{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/61581297060581/posts/a-court-filing-submitted-on-april-6-2026-by-hunter-bidens-attorney-barry-coburn-/122128332639043235/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/61581297060581/posts/a-court-filing-submitted-on-april-6-2026-by-hunter-bidens-attorney-barry-coburn-/122128332639043235/","title":"Daily.Bharat.News","description":"A court filing submitted on April 6, 2026, by Hunter Biden’s attorney Barry Coburn in a Washington, D.C. lawsuit from his former law firm Winston & Strawn states that Hunter Biden now “lives abroad”...","language":"en","text":"A court filing submitted on April 6, 2026, by Hunter Biden’s attorney Barry Coburn in a Washington, D.C. lawsuit from his former law firm Winston & Strawn states that Hunter Biden now “lives abroad” and “cannot afford” to pay his outstanding legal bills.\n\nThe firm claims he owes fees “substantially in excess of $50,000” related to his prior tax and gun cases. The filing describes him as “impecunious” (penniless) and notes that neither he nor his current lawyers can cover discovery costs such as billing consultants or e-discovery vendors.\n\nThis aligns with Hunter Biden’s own earlier statements claiming roughly $17 million (about ₹158 crore) in debt, mostly from legal expenses tied to his federal cases. Some media reports describe him as having “quietly bolted” from the U.S., though the filing itself simply states he lives abroad without specifying the location or suggesting he is evading authorities.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n6 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2978.058290998888,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}